        "title": "Expert Backed Review Summary",
        "text": "<p>JiYu NAD+ Hydrating Face Moisturizer has gained significant attention for its promise to simplify skincare by combining hydration, brightening, and anti-aging benefits in a single cream. The formula features NAD+, niacinamide, ceramides, five molecular weights of hyaluronic acid, vitamin C derivatives, and ferulic acid to support moisture retention, barrier function, and overall skin radiance. Users frequently praise its lightweight yet nourishing texture, noting that it absorbs quickly, layers well under makeup, and leaves skin feeling softer and plumper. The fragrance-free, vegan formulation also appeals to individuals with ingredient sensitivities. However, some of the product's more ambitious marketing claims warrant caution. While users often report improved hydration and smoother texture, evidence supporting topical NAD+ as a breakthrough anti-aging ingredient remains limited. The moisturizer is also relatively expensive for its 50 ml size, and critics question whether it can genuinely replace an entire multi-step routine. Online communities have additionally raised concerns regarding the brand's aggressive promotional tactics and transparency, although these concerns relate more to marketing than product safety.</p>",
        "body_align": "center",
